# Whitelist strategy: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-admit only the Convos
# customization layer. Anything not explicitly whitelisted never reaches git —
# which is what keeps tokens, OAuth secrets, personal data, and the upstream
# Hermes app out of the repo.

/*

# ── The Convos layer ─────────────────────────────────────────────
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/SOUL.md
!/config.example.yaml

!/scripts/
!/hooks/
# skills: only the travel pack (the rest ship with Hermes)
!/skills/
/skills/*
!/skills/travel/

# ── Never these, even inside whitelisted dirs ────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# one-off backfill/fix scripts carry real names & phone numbers
scripts/backfill_*.py
scripts/set_laura.py
scripts/link_train_trip14.py

# skills may cache creds/artifacts locally
skills/**/node_modules/
skills/**/package-lock.json
skills/**/.env
skills/**/*token*
skills/**/*secret*
skills/**/cookies*
skills/**/__pycache__/
skills/.*
skills/travel/**/data/*.db

# ── Explicitly called out (already covered by /*, but make it loud) ──
# .env                  — PHOTON_* secrets
# auth.json             — Hermes auth
# google_token.json     — Google OAuth token
# google_client_secret.json
# data/                 — trips.db: real trips, phones, names
# sessions/ state.db*   — chat transcripts
# logs/ cron/ memories/ — runtime
# hermes-agent/         — upstream app, not ours to publish
